WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.208 --> 00:00:18.591
Hook always carried a bottle of poison in his pocket to make sure he could never be captured

2
00:00:18.631 --> 00:00:23.853
alive. He had made the poison himself, so he knew it was effective.

3
00:00:24.953 --> 00:00:31.096
Hook added five drops to Peter's medicine and rubbed his hook against his hand with excitement.

4
00:00:33.076 --> 00:00:39.119
Then, with a triumphant look at his victim, he slid his way back up and out of the

5
00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:41.801
tree. Peter slept on.

6
00:00:42.821 --> 00:00:48.184
He knew nothing about the massacre of his Indian friends or about the capture of Wendy and the

7
00:00:48.224 --> 00:00:55.788
boys. He didn't know about Hook coming into his home or about the dangerous cup of medicine standing

8
00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:56.449
on the shelf.

9
00:00:57.609 --> 00:01:02.372
Finally he was awakened by a soft, careful knock on the door of his tunnel.

10
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:06.498
Peter grabbed his dagger and shouted, "Who is it?"

11
00:01:06.518 --> 00:01:10.480
"Let me in quickly, Peter!"

12
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.622
said Tinker Bell in her bell-like voice.

13
00:01:14.843 --> 00:01:18.144
Peter opened the round door and she flew into the room.

14
00:01:19.425 --> 00:01:23.027
Her little face was flushed and her dress stained with mud.

15
00:01:23.047 --> 00:01:25.088
"What is it, Tink?"

16
00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:26.329
asked Peter.

17
00:01:26.349 --> 00:01:30.071
"Oh, you could never guess!"

18
00:01:30.771 --> 00:01:31.432
she cried.

19
00:01:32.588 --> 00:01:36.789
Then she told him the terrible news about how Wendy and the boys had been captured.

20
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:41.531
As Peter listened, his heart beat faster and faster.

21
00:01:42.651 --> 00:01:44.631
Wendy was tied up and on the pirate ship?

22
00:01:45.352 --> 00:01:46.632
He had to rescue her!

23
00:01:47.792 --> 00:01:50.773
Already he had forgotten how angry he was with her.

24
00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:56.215
Wanting to please her, he went to get the medicine off the shelf.

25
00:01:56.235 --> 00:01:58.395
"Don't do that!"

26
00:01:59.036 --> 00:02:01.520
screamed Tinker Bell.

27
00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:06.805
She had heard Hook muttering as he went through the forest, and she had learned about the poison.

28
00:02:06.825 --> 00:02:08.626
"Why not?"

29
00:02:09.207 --> 00:02:09.807
asked Peter.

30
00:02:11.348 --> 00:02:12.769
"Your medicine is poisoned.

31
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.772
Hook did it while you slept," she said.

32
00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:18.794
"Don't be silly," Peter said.

33
00:02:18.814 --> 00:02:21.577
"You know that no grown-up can enter here."

34
00:02:22.557 --> 00:02:27.782
Tinker Bell could not explain how Hook had done it because she didn't know the secret of Slightly's

35
00:02:27.842 --> 00:02:36.534
tree. "Besides," said Peter, not wanting to admit that he had cried and fallen asleep, "I never fell

36
00:02:36.594 --> 00:02:39.434
asleep." He raised the cup to his lips.

37
00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:44.636
Like a bolt of lightning, Tinker Bell flew between his lips and the liquid.

38
00:02:45.556 --> 00:02:47.316
She drank the whole cup.

39
00:02:47.336 --> 00:02:50.097
"How dare you drink my medicine!"

40
00:02:50.657 --> 00:02:51.257
he yelled.

41
00:02:52.558 --> 00:02:54.298
But Tinker Bell did not answer.

42
00:02:55.359 --> 00:02:58.059
Already she was fluttering dizzily in the air.

43
00:02:58.079 --> 00:03:00.580
"What's the matter with you?"

44
00:03:01.264 --> 00:03:03.265
asked Peter, suddenly afraid.

45
00:03:03.285 --> 00:03:07.067
"I told you," she said softly.

46
00:03:07.087 --> 00:03:11.470
"It was poisoned, and now I'm going to die."

47
00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:17.473
"Oh, Tink, you drank the poison to save my life," he said.

48
00:03:17.493 --> 00:03:19.735
"Why did you do it?"

49
00:03:19.755 --> 00:03:23.117
"Don't be silly, Peter," she whispered.

50
00:03:23.137 --> 00:03:24.477
"You know why."

51
00:03:25.678 --> 00:03:28.780
Tinker Bell flew slowly to her nook and lay on her bed.

52
00:03:30.332 --> 00:03:33.734
As Peter watched, her light grew fainter and fainter.

53
00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:39.056
For the second time in just a few hours, Peter began to cry.

54
00:03:40.216 --> 00:03:44.298
Tink's voice, now very low, stopped his tears for a moment.

55
00:03:44.318 --> 00:03:51.201
"If enough children believe in fairies," she told him, "I know I will get well again."

56
00:03:53.002 --> 00:03:56.864
There were no children left in the house, but Peter knew what he could do.

57
00:03:57.952 --> 00:04:00.533
He called out to all the children who might be dreaming.

58
00:04:01.513 --> 00:04:06.494
Peter knew that in their dreams children were nearer to Neverland than anyone imagined.

59
00:04:06.514 --> 00:04:08.855
"Do you believe?"

60
00:04:09.455 --> 00:04:10.115
he shouted.

61
00:04:10.135 --> 00:04:13.956
"If you do, please clap your hands!"

62
00:04:15.237 --> 00:04:18.898
Never before had Peter said "please" in such a sincere way.

63
00:04:20.158 --> 00:04:24.659
He stretched out his arms and cried, "Don't let Tinker Bell die!"

64
00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.029
Suddenly there was a roar of clapping from around the world.

65
00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:36.833
And as parents all over rushed to their children's rooms to see what was the matter, Tinker Bell

66
00:04:36.953 --> 00:04:38.333
sat up in bed.

67
00:04:39.394 --> 00:04:41.215
Her light was bright once again.

68
00:04:41.835 --> 00:04:43.576
Peter had saved her!
